From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: keep MPPE SGMII in-band framing

The IPQ53xx MPPE vendor stack drives link state from the external PHY but
leaves the UNIPHY SGMII channel in Qualcomm/Atheros in-band framing
mode. The working vendor state keeps PCS_MII_FORCE_MODE clear while using
the PHY link event to update clocks and pulse the channel adapter reset.

Phylink's out-of-band mode currently sets PCS_MII_FORCE_MODE, which
changes the working MPPE PCS control value from 0x844 to 0x84c. Keep
force mode clear for MPPE SGMII while still using the PHY-driven phylink
state and link-up callback. Log the MPPE PCS state after the link-up reset
while bring-up is in progress.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -581,7 +581,8 @@ static int ipq_pcs_config_sgmii(struct ipq_pcs *qpcs,
 	}
 
 	/* Set AN mode or force mode */
-	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED)
+	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED ||
+	    (qpcs->mppe && interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII))
 		ret = regmap_clear_bits(qpcs->regmap,
 					PCS_MII_CTRL(index), PCS_MII_FORCE_MODE);
 	else
@@ -743,8 +744,22 @@ static int ipq_pcs_link_up_config_sgmii(struct ipq_pcs *qpcs,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return regmap_set_bits(qpcs->regmap,
-			       PCS_MII_CTRL(index), PCS_MII_ADPT_RESET);
+	ret = regmap_set_bits(qpcs->regmap,
+			      PCS_MII_CTRL(index), PCS_MII_ADPT_RESET);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (qpcs->mppe) {
+		unsigned int ctrl, sts;
+
+		if (!regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MII_CTRL(index), &ctrl) &&
+		    !regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MII_STS(index), &sts))
+			dev_info(qpcs->dev,
+				 "MPPE SGMII link-up: neg=%u speed=%d ctrl=%#x sts=%#x\n",
+				 neg_mode, speed, ctrl, sts);
+	}
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int ipq_pcs_link_up_config_2500basex(struct ipq_pcs *qpcs, int speed)
